      "text": "To determine the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to find integers \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) such that:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q)\n\\]\n\nExpanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients with \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\), we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\np + q = b \\quad \\text{and} \\quad pq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find pairs of integers \\( (p, q) \\) whose product is 2008. First, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nThe factor pairs of 2008 are:\n\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nWe now calculate \\( b = p + q \\) for each pair:\n\n1. For \\( (1, 2008) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\( (-1, -2008) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = -1 - 2008 = -2009\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\( (2, 1004) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\( (-2, -1004) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = -2 - 1004 = -1006\n   \\]\n\n5. For \\( (4, 502) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = 4 + 502 = 506\n   \\]\n\n6. For \\( (-4, -502) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = -4 - 502 = -506\n   \\]\n\n7. For \\( (8, 251) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = 8 + 251 = 259\n   \\]\n\n8. For \\( (-8, -251) \\):\n   \\[\n   p + q = -8 - 251 = -259\n   \\]\n\nAmong all these values of \\( b \\), the smallest positive integer is 2009. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2009}\n\\]",
