      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) such that the quadratic polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express the polynomial in the form \\((x + p)(x + q)\\), where \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers. This gives us:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients, we get:\n\n\\[\nb = p + q \\quad \\text{and} \\quad pq = 2008\n\\]\n\nWe need to find pairs of integers \\((p, q)\\) such that their product is 2008 and then determine the smallest positive value of \\( b = p + q \\).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nThe factor pairs of 2008 are: \\((1, 2008)\\), \\((2, 1004)\\), \\((4, 502)\\), \\((8, 251)\\), \\((-1, -2008)\\), \\((-2, -1004)\\), \\((-4, -502)\\), \\((-8, -251)\\).\n\nWe will calculate \\( b = p + q \\) for each pair:\n\n1. For \\((p, q) = (1, 2008)\\), \\( b = 1 + 2008 = 2009 \\).\n2. For \\((p, q) = (2, 1004)\\), \\( b = 2 + 1004 = 1006 \\).\n3. For \\((p, q) = (4, 502)\\), \\( b = 4 + 502 = 506 \\).\n4. For \\((p, q) = (8, 251)\\), \\( b = 8 + 251 = 259 \\).\n5. For \\((p, q) = (-1, -2008)\\), \\( b = -1 + (-2008) = -2009 \\) (not positive).\n6. For \\((p, q) = (-2, -1004)\\), \\( b = -2 + (-1004) = -1006 \\) (not positive).\n7. For \\((p, q) = (-4, -502)\\), \\( b = -4 + (-502) = -506 \\) (not positive).\n8. For \\((p, q) = (-8, -251)\\), \\( b = -8 + (-251) = -259 \\) (not positive).\n\nThe smallest positive value of \\( b \\) is from the pair \\((p, q) = (8, 251)\\), which gives \\( b = 259 \\).\n\nThus, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
