      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) such that the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we start by assuming the factorization form:\n\n\\[\nx^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q)\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers. Expanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p+q)x + pq\n\\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients with the original quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\), we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n1. \\( p + q = b \\)\n2. \\( pq = 2008 \\)\n\nWe need to find pairs of integers \\( (p, q) \\) whose product is 2008. First, we list the factor pairs of 2008:\n\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nThe factor pairs are: \\((1, 2008)\\), \\((2, 1004)\\), \\((4, 502)\\), \\((8, 251)\\), \\((-1, -2008)\\), \\((-2, -1004)\\), \\((-4, -502)\\), \\((-8, -251)\\).\n\nWe will evaluate each pair to find the corresponding values of \\( b = p + q \\):\n\n1. For the pair \\((1, 2008)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 1 + 2008 = 2009\n   \\]\n\n2. For the pair \\((2, 1004)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 2 + 1004 = 1006\n   \\]\n\n3. For the pair \\((4, 502)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 4 + 502 = 506\n   \\]\n\n4. For the pair \\((8, 251)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = 8 + 251 = 259\n   \\]\n\n5. For the pair \\((-1, -2008)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = -1 + (-2008) = -2009\n   \\]\n\n6. For the pair \\((-2, -1004)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = -2 + (-1004) = -1006\n   \\]\n\n7. For the pair \\((-4, -502)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = -4 + (-502) = -506\n   \\]\n\n8. For the pair \\((-8, -251)\\):\n   \\[\n   b = -8 + (-251) = -259\n   \\]\n\nAmong these values, the smallest positive integer for \\( b \\) is 2. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
